# Code Quality Rules

## Early Returns — Guard Clauses First

```typescript
// ✅ Validate/guard at the top, happy path at the bottom
async function processDownload(userId: string, downloadId: string) {
  if (!userId)     throw new ValidationError('userId required')
  if (!downloadId) throw new ValidationError('downloadId required')

  const user = await UserRepository.findById(userId)
  if (!user)     throw new NotFoundError('User not found')
  if (!user.isActive) throw new ForbiddenError('Account inactive')

  // happy path — no deep nesting
  const download = await DownloadRepository.create({ userId, downloadId })
  return download
}

// ❌ Deeply nested — hard to read
async function processDownload(userId: string, downloadId: string) {
  if (userId) {
    if (downloadId) {
      const user = await UserRepository.findById(userId)
      if (user) {
        if (user.isActive) {
          return await DownloadRepository.create({ userId, downloadId })
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## DRY — Don't Repeat Yourself

```typescript
// ✅ Extract repeated patterns into utilities
// If the same logic appears in 2+ places, extract it

// ✅ Shared validation schemas — define once, import everywhere
export const PaginationSchema = z.object({
  page:  z.coerce.number().int().min(1).default(1),
  limit: z.coerce.number().int().min(1).max(100).default(20),
})

// ✅ Shared response helpers
export const ok  = <T>(res: Response, data: T, status = 200) =>
  res.status(status).json({ success: true, data })

export const err = (res: Response, code: string, message: string, status = 400) =>
  res.status(status).json({ success: false, error: { code, message } })
```

## Variable Naming — Auxiliary Verbs

```typescript
// ✅ Boolean variables use is/has/can/should prefix
const isLoading   = true
const hasError    = false
const canEdit     = user.role === 'admin'
const isStreakActive = streak.current > 0

// ✅ Async operations — use past tense or clear verb forms
const fetchedUser  = await UserRepository.findById(id)
const createdMode  = await ModeService.create(data)

// ✅ Arrays/collections — plural nouns
const sessions:  ModeSession[]  = []
const downloads: Download[]     = []
const insights:  AIInsight[]    = []
```

## No Magic Values

```typescript
// ❌ Magic numbers and strings
setTimeout(fn, 900000)
if (streak > 7) { }
jwt.sign(payload, secret, { expiresIn: '900s' })

// ✅ Named constants
const METRICS_CACHE_TTL_MS    = 15 * 60 * 1000    // 15 minutes
const STREAK_MILESTONE_DAYS   = [7, 14, 30, 60, 100]
const JWT_ACCESS_TTL          = '15m'

setTimeout(fn, METRICS_CACHE_TTL_MS)
if (STREAK_MILESTONE_DAYS.includes(streak)) { }
jwt.sign(payload, secret, { expiresIn: JWT_ACCESS_TTL })
```

## Const by Default

```typescript
// ✅ const unless reassignment is necessary
const userId = req.user.id
const sessions = await SessionRepository.findByUserId(userId)

// ✅ let only when reassigning
let retries = 0
while (retries < 3) {
  retries++
}

// ❌ Never var
var userId = req.user.id
```

## No Console Logs in Production Code

```typescript
// ❌ Never leave console.log in committed code
console.log('user:', user)

// ✅ Use structured logger
import { logger } from '../utils/logger'
logger.info('User session started', { userId, modeId })
logger.error('AI router failed', { error: err.message, model })
logger.warn('Rate limit approaching', { userId, count })

// ✅ Logger wraps a library (pino recommended) — structured JSON output
// api/src/utils/logger.ts
import pino from 'pino'
export const logger = pino({ level: env.NODE_ENV === 'production' ? 'info' : 'debug' })
```

## Never Swallow Errors

```typescript
// ❌ Silent catch — error disappears
try {
  await AIQueue.add('generate-insight', data)
} catch (err) {
  // do nothing
}

// ✅ Always log or re-throw
try {
  await AIQueue.add('generate-insight', data)
} catch (err) {
  logger.error('Failed to queue AI job', { error: (err as Error).message, data })
  // re-throw if the caller needs to know
  throw err
}
```

## File Length — Single Responsibility

```
If a file exceeds ~200 lines, it probably has more than one responsibility.
Split it. Each file should do one thing.

controller file    → route handlers only (no business logic)
service file       → one domain's business logic
repository file    → one model's DB operations
hook file          → one piece of React state logic
component file     → one UI component
```

## Comments — Why, Not What

```typescript
// ❌ Comments that describe what the code does (the code already says this)
// Increment counter
count++

// ❌ Commented-out code — delete it, git has history
// const oldLogic = await OldService.do()

// ✅ Comments that explain WHY — context the code can't express
// Redis TTL is 30s not 15s here because the metrics endpoint is called
// on every WebSocket reconnect and we need to absorb reconnect storms
await redis.setex(key, 30, JSON.stringify(metrics))

// ✅ TODO comments must include a ticket reference or date
// TODO(2026-03-15): Replace with native groupBy when Node 22 is stable
```

## Immutability — Prefer Immutable Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ Spread instead of mutate
const updatedMode = { ...mode, isActive: true, updatedAt: new Date().toISOString() }

// ✅ Map/filter/reduce instead of push/splice
const activeSessions = sessions.filter(s => !s.endedAt)
const sessionIds = sessions.map(s => s.id)

// ❌ Mutating function parameters
function normalise(user: User) {
  user.email = user.email.toLowerCase()  // mutates the input object
  return user
}

// ✅ Return new object
function normalise(user: User): User {
  return { ...user, email: user.email.toLowerCase() }
}
```
